[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   Step 103 -- RTG mid-life degradation control.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   Step 098 found that Voyager 1's three independent MHW-RTG units
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   decline coherently across the heliopause window (--0.4 per cent
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   excess vs the 13-26 yr interior baseline), while Voyager 2's two
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   surviving units diverge -- and noted the remaining loophole
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   explicitly: the excursion could be undocumented mid-life MHW
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   aging, not a field-linked transition.  Three of the five units
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   share one craft, so unit coherence alone cannot separate a
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   common-mode aging process from a common-mode field coupling.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   This step supplies the missing control without new assumptions:
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   the telemetry record's own wander defines what undocumented aging
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   can produce.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   T1  Ramp-placebo scan.  The saturating-ramp statistic of step
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   098 (c0 + A*clip((t-t0)/w, 0, 1) fitted to the mean-unit
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   excess curve) is evaluated for EVERY onset t0 in 14-40 yr
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   and width w in {3,5,7,9} yr, not only in the boundary
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   region.  The crossing-aligned ramp is compared against the
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   full-record amplitude distribution: if equally deep coherent
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   ramps occur at placebo epochs, ordinary aging explains the
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   excursion and the result stays a bound; if the
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   crossing-window ramp is extreme, the candidate tightens.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   T2  All-negative coherence window.  The fraction of grid epochs
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   on which all three V1 units sit below baseline is computed
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   on a +-3 yr window centred at the heliopause and on every
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   equal-length sliding window of the record -- the empirical
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   null for three-unit sign coherence.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   T3  Vintage-matched control.  Voyager 2's two functioning units
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   are the same MHW design with the same 1977 beginning-of-
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   mission epoch: whatever generic mid-life aging does to V1's
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   units at mission-year 29-37 it must also do to V2's at the
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   SAME mission years (V2 was still inside the heliosphere and
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   outside both field lobes then).  The identical (t0, w) ramp
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   is fitted to the V2 mean-unit excess over the identical
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   window; a V2 ramp of equal amplitude would convict common-
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   mode aging, while a flat or incoherent V2 record makes the
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   V1 excursion location-specific.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   T4  Leave-one-unit-out.  The crossing-window ramp amplitude is
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   recomputed for each two-unit subset of V1, testing whether
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   the coherence survives dropping any single unit.
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   T5  Unit-spread audit.  The cross-unit dispersion sigma(t) of
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   the three V1 excess curves during the excursion is compared
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   with its full-record distribution: a genuine common-mode
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   excursion keeps the spread at its usual level rather than
[2026-09-20 12:19:47 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 103]   inflating it.
